Z||000000||grinthock||08-01-2001||08:04 PM||||Can you guys help me out?  On the MSD site there is a bunch of different MSD coils, is there one I MUST use?  Or something reccomended?  I feel like a moron asking because I know it's just a coil!  Do we NEED to use a HEI coil?   I am so confused.<p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Capt Fiero||08-01-2001||09:14 PM||||Ok for V6 You want coil ## 8226<BR> <P>( this is a message that I just sent to someone else asking about doing a full MSD Conversion, I included parts numbers and such)Well if you want to go hole hog on a budget, I would recommend, <BR> <BR>MSD Coil ##  8226 If you buy anything buy this first.  It is a direct replacement for your stock coil, it has GM factory connectors on it and will spruce up a stock weak ignition.<BR> <BR>MSD Ignition Box 6A ## 6200 the 6A is the same as the 6AL it just does not have a rev limiter.  If you are going to go nuts and have tons of money to spend you can look into the MSD Digital Series at close to 1000$ that will do just about anything you want, including control NOS kits and you can even retard your ignition timing from a knob on your dash.<BR> <BR>MSD Super Conductor Wires, 8.8 mm 40-50 ohm per foot resistance  these are pretty much the best wires on the market for the money spent without going to a full on race wire, and actually many race cars do use these. (sorry there is no part number for the Fiero, you have to get a custom V8 set. Then  cut to fit, meaning you have to build the wires yourself, it is not a hard job it takes about 2hrs to do.<BR> <BR>and last but not least MSD Harness Adapter ## 8876  This makes it a plug and play install.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=32415"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||08-01-2001||10:03 PM||||Well priced it all out at SUMMIT for those of you who are wondering what a complete ignition system for a Fiero is (minus distributor)<P> MSD-31179   MSD 8.5 mm Super Conductor Wire Sets   $71.39  <BR>     <BR>   MSD-6200   MSD Ignition Control Units   $131.95  <BR>     <BR>   MSD-8226   MSD Blaster GM Coil   $38.95  <BR>     <BR>   MSD-8876   MSD Universal Wiring Harness   $27.95 <P><BR>NOT too bad!!! Total is 270.24 that's $360 Canadian $405.36     <BR>||||reg||1
